From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: fix ROCCAT Juke sticky-mixer quirk leaving
 playback silenced

The ROCCAT Juke 7.1 (CM6206-based, 1e7d:371e) Playback Volume feature
unit (FU 13) always reports the same GET_CUR raw value regardless of
what SET_CUR writes, e.g.:

  usb 1-4.3.2.2: 13:0: sticky mixer values (0/6096/48 => 5376), disabling
  check MIXER_GET_CUR_BROKEN if you believe the mixer is non-sticky

check_sticky_volume_control() in sound/usb/mixer.c can't tell a truly
sticky (non-functional) mixer apart from one where only the readback
is broken, so without a hint it gates registration of the control
entirely (-ENODEV, "disabling"). On the Juke the hardware volume is
in fact tunable via SET_CUR - only GET_CUR is constant.

Part 1 (sound/usb/quirks.c): add a DEVICE_FLG() entry with
QUIRK_FLAG_MIXER_GET_CUR_BROKEN, exactly as the in-source hint
suggests, so the sticky check takes the non-fatal path
(get_cur_broken=1, GET_CUR served from cache) instead of refusing to
register the control.

Part 2 (sound/usb/mixer.c): that alone isn't enough. Once
get_min_max_with_quirks() sees check_sticky_volume_control() return
non-zero for the get_cur_broken case, it takes the "no_checks" path,
which clears cval->cached and skips restoring the probed "saved"
value - unlike the true-non-sticky success path, which restores it.
init_cur_mix_raw() then runs for every channel, tries to read back a
current value to seed the cache, and fails every time (get_cur_broken
makes every uncached read return -ENXIO by design, and also silences
the warning for this exact case). Its fallback on that failure is to
explicitly command the hardware to cval->min:

  snd_usb_set_cur_mix_value(cval, ch, idx, cval->min);

So on every boot the driver silences the Juke outright - a real
SET_CUR to the DAC, not a display/caching artifact. PipeWire's own
volume model never observes this, so it doesn't proactively re-push
anything; the first real SET_CUR only happens once the user manually
touches the GUI slider, which is why playback appeared to only start
above a specific level (wherever the slider happened to be sitting) -
that value was never a meaningful threshold.

For get_cur_broken mixers - where SET_CUR is known-good and only the
readback lies - defaulting to cval->min on the forced-init path is the
wrong safe default. Use cval->max instead, matching the philosophy the
same function already applies at its "sticky:" fallback ("so that a
soft mixer can still reach the maximum hardware volume"). This changes
nothing for every other, non-quirked device: their get_cur_broken is
always 0, so they keep defaulting to cval->min exactly as before.

Reported by RakuOS (a downstream Linux distribution) users running
its kernel-p03 build.

Signed-off-by: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
---
 sound/usb/mixer.c  | 4 +++-
 sound/usb/quirks.c | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/usb/mixer.c b/sound/usb/mixer.c
--- a/sound/usb/mixer.c
+++ b/sound/usb/mixer.c
@@ -1229,7 +1229,10 @@ static void init_cur_mix_raw(struct usb_mixer_elem_info *cval, int ch, int idx
 			       "%d:%d: failed to get current value for ch %d (%d)\n",
 			       cval->head.id, mixer_ctrl_intf(cval->head.mixer),
 			       ch, err);
-	snd_usb_set_cur_mix_value(cval, ch, idx, cval->min);
+	/* GET_CUR-broken-but-SET_CUR-effective devices: prefer max over
+	 * silence, we just can't confirm the real current value. */
+	snd_usb_set_cur_mix_value(cval, ch, idx,
+				   cval->get_cur_broken ? cval->max : cval->min);
 }
 
 /*
diff --git a/sound/usb/quirks.c b/sound/usb/quirks.c
--- a/sound/usb/quirks.c
+++ b/sound/usb/quirks.c
@@ -2432,6 +2432,8 @@
 		   QUIRK_FLAG_GET_SAMPLE_RATE | QUIRK_FLAG_MIC_RES_16),
 	DEVICE_FLG(0x1bcf, 0x2283, /* NexiGo N930AF FHD Webcam */
 		   QUIRK_FLAG_GET_SAMPLE_RATE | QUIRK_FLAG_MIC_RES_16),
+	DEVICE_FLG(0x1e7d, 0x371e, /* ROCCAT Juke 7.1 */
+		   QUIRK_FLAG_MIXER_GET_CUR_BROKEN),
 	DEVICE_FLG(0x1ff7, 0x0f81, /* SC13A Webcam */
 		   QUIRK_FLAG_GET_SAMPLE_RATE),
 	DEVICE_FLG(0x2040, 0x7200, /* Hauppauge HVR-950Q */
--
2.49.0
